title: The Mark Falls
subtitle: A thousand marks to the dollar.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 8
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('A thousand marks to the dollar', 3);
Q.inflation = Math.min(100, Q.inflation + 6);
Q.stability -= 4;
!}

= The Mark Falls

In January a dollar cost two hundred marks. At the end of August it costs more than a thousand. Shops mark up their prices on Monday and again on Thursday. Hugo Stinnes buys mines, hotels and newspapers with loans he will repay in worthless paper, and in the markets of Berlin and Leipzig women turn on the traders they think are hoarding.

- @committees: Form control committees to check the shops.
- @scales: Fight in the unions for wages that rise with prices.
- @marches: Lead the unemployed on the town halls.

@committees
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Workers and housewives with price lists, starting in Saxony. It builds something that lasts.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('councils');
RG.district('saxony', {loyalty: 5, members: 0.04});
RG.district('thuringia', {loyalty: 5});
Q.e22_inflation_line = 1;
Q.worker_support += 4;
!}

The first control committees go from shop to shop in Chemnitz and Gera with lists of fair prices. Some shopkeepers lower them. Some call the police, and the police do not always come.

@scales
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Slow work in the metalworkers' union, and respect for it.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids work inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('union_work');
Q.e22_inflation_line = 3;
Q.spd_relation += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Our members move resolution after resolution for a sliding scale of wages. By the autumn some big works pay a weekly bonus tied to the price of bread.

@marches
subtitle: Food for some, prison for others, in Halle and the Ruhr.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0 or ultraleft_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('halle', {militancy: 8, repression: 8});
RG.district('ruhr', {militancy: 8, repression: 8});
Q.e22_inflation_line = 2;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Thousands of unemployed march on the town halls of Halle and Gelsenkirchen. Two markets are plundered. Most of those arrested are ours.
